# Local secrets for `wrangler dev` (copy to .dev.vars; never committed). Production: `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
# Signs sessions, match tickets and the Worker <-> Durable Object internal header: a long random string.
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Required outside local dev (POST /api/guest answers 503 'turnstile_unconfigured' without it on a deploy).
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=
# Comma-separated browser origins allowed for CORS and WebSocket upgrades (unset = '*' / any Origin, dev only).
# VITE_ORIGINS=https://your-game.example
# Local OAuth testing only: the origin the provider redirects back to (the Vite page, which proxies
# /api to this Worker), e.g. http://localhost:5173. Production uses the request's own origin.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# Community nodes (nodes/), optional: without the control key (and the NODES binding with its R2
# buckets) the Worker never sends a match to a node. The private half of nodes/.keys/control.json
# (`npm run keys` in nodes/); its public half is the NODE_CONTROL_PUBLIC_KEY var.
# NODE_CONTROL_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The project's account ids (16 hex characters each), comma-separated: their nodes are trusted.
# NODE_TRUSTED_OPERATORS=
# A webhook URL the node control plane posts its ALERT lines to.
# NODE_ALERT_WEBHOOK=
